# Whitelist-based: exclude everything, then include what's needed
*

# Root package files (needed for workspace resolution)
!package.json
!package-lock.json

# Server package
!packages/server/

# Workspace packages the server imports at runtime (#8133). Only the exports
# map and the committed build are needed, not their src/ or tests/.
!packages/protocol/package.json
!packages/protocol/dist/
!packages/store-core/package.json
!packages/store-core/dist/
# #8151 — the dashboard-builder stage additionally needs store-core's raw TS
# source: its "." export (unlike "./crypto") resolves to src/index.ts, which
# Vite transforms directly rather than importing a build.
!packages/store-core/src/

# #8151 — the dashboard-builder stage. Whitelisted whole (minus its own
# dev-time node_modules/dist below) rather than file-by-file: unlike the
# server, this is Vite/TypeScript source that changes shape often, and the
# `docker` path filter in ci.yml already re-runs the smoke test on any change
# under these two directories, so a missed file here fails loudly in CI
# rather than silently shipping a stale dashboard.
!packages/dashboard/
!packages/design-tokens/

# Entrypoint script
!scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh

# Exclude server artifacts that slipped through
packages/server/node_modules
packages/server/tests
packages/server/coverage
# Dev-only lints. They are never run in the image, and lint-entry-point-guard.mjs
# imports repo-root scripts/lib/, which the image does not copy — so shipping
# them would put a module with an unresolvable import inside the container
# (inert, but pointless). fix-node-pty-helper.js is the one the build needs.
packages/server/scripts/lint-*
packages/server/scripts/lib

# Exclude dashboard dev-time artifacts that slipped through (a local build or
# `npm install` on the host would otherwise leak its own node_modules/dist
# into the build context ahead of the dashboard-builder stage's own ci/build).
packages/dashboard/node_modules
packages/dashboard/dist
packages/dashboard/coverage

# #8151 review (S5): more dev-time artifacts the whitelists above would
# otherwise leak into the build context on a machine that has run the
# dashboard/design-tokens packages locally.
# Never leak a contributor's local secrets into the image or build context —
# a whitelisted package directory (!packages/dashboard/, etc.) would
# otherwise sweep in any .env file a developer keeps there for local runs.
**/.env*
# repo-memory's local cache; Vite's own dev-server cache dir (distinct from
# node_modules/.vite, already excluded above via the node_modules blacklist).
packages/dashboard/.repo-memory
packages/dashboard/.vite
# tsc --incremental build-info files (not needed to build; not reproducible
# across machines, so shipping one would be pure bytes-with-no-purpose).
**/*.tsbuildinfo
packages/design-tokens/node_modules
packages/design-tokens/coverage
# Generalizes the two specific coverage excludes above — any whitelisted
# package could grow a coverage/ dir from a local `npm test --coverage` run.
**/coverage
# Dashboard test files are not imported by production code (`vite build`
# never reaches them) and are the bulk of packages/dashboard's file count —
# excluding them keeps the build context small without touching what the
# build actually needs. Verified: the dashboard-builder stage still builds
# with these excluded (#8151 review).
packages/dashboard/src/**/*.test.ts
packages/dashboard/src/**/*.test.tsx
packages/dashboard/src/test-setup.ts

# #8151 review (C2 nit) — packages/server/src/dashboard-next/ is the Tauri
# desktop bundle's copy of this SAME dashboard (see http-routes.js's bundle
# fallback path) and is gitignored, so it does not exist in a fresh checkout
# — but Docker's build context is NOT git-aware, only .dockerignore-aware.
# On a machine that has ever built the Tauri desktop app, this directory
# exists on disk and `!packages/server/` above would sweep it straight into
# the image, carrying a second, independently-stale copy of the exact same
# <title>Chroxy Dashboard</title> marker check 5 looks for — a local build
# could pass the smoke test against a dashboard this PR's dashboard-builder
# stage never touched.
packages/server/src/dashboard-next
